    {
      "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
      "text": "The number of unique 5-player lineups is vast, and many will have very limited playing time, especially when considering transitions between specific lineups. This will limit the statistical power to detect effects for individual lineup changes or even aggregate effects across many diverse changes."
    },
    {
      "code": "EXPOSURE_SPARSITY",
      "text": "Specific lineup combinations and the transitions between them will suffer from sparse data, making it difficult to get reliable estimates. This is exacerbated by the need to control for many factors."
    },
    {
      "code": "RTM_SELECTION",
      "text": "If lineups are changed in response to extreme performance (good or bad), observed changes in shot mix might be due to regression to the mean rather than a true personnel effect."
